{
  "dataset": "Symptom quality (症狀性質) controlled vocabulary",
  "policy": [
    "Values for a symptom card clinical_attributes.quality. This axis carries the most diagnostic weight in TCM, so it is a closed set, not free text.",
    "inference_hint is NEVER a rule. It is a direction to consider, and it is modulated by location, disease course and accompanying signs — 脹 in the hypochondrium and 脹 in the lower abdomen do not carry the same weight. The actual reasoning, with its own sources, lives in a symptom card differentiation[].",
    "target_pattern_ids[] is left EMPTY in Batch A on purpose. Filling it now would mint pattern links from a vocabulary file rather than from a sourced clinical judgement — which is the failure this whole layer is built to avoid. The 15 pilot cards decide whether these hints hold.",
    "inference_hint_only: true on every entry. No consumer may treat this file as a diagnosis rule.",
    "IDs are ASCII (D10). Adding a value is a schema change: this file, then the validator, then data."
  ],
  "created": "2026-08-06",
  "applies_to": "sym.* records via clinical_attributes.quality",
